WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:07.690
NEAL MUELLER: Hi, I'm Neal
Mueller on the Geographic

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.639
Expansion Team.

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:10.180
We build the technical
infrastructure

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.640
that powers Google and
Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.620
This includes new
regions, points

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.690
of presence, solar
and wind farms,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.420
and terrestrial and
submarine cable networks.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.510
I'm here today to tell you about
a new amazing region in Sydney.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:23.770
It's now open.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.270
This isn't our first
region in Asia.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.060
We also have Singapore,
Taiwan and Tokyo.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.980
Our global network
connects all of our regions

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.470
together, along with our
100 points of presence

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.822
all over the world.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:35.530
The Google network is
the largest network

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.520
of any public cloud provider.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.230
Now that I've told
you about our network,

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.650
let's talk about the
Sydney region itself.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.900
For the first time
ever, GCP users

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.540
can process and store
data locally in Australia.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.510
As you can see from
this list of services,

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.660
the services include
compute, big data, storage

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.399
and networking.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:55.815
You can find a whole lot more
about the services in Sydney

00:00:55.815 --> 00:01:00.310
at cloud.google.com
/about/locations.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.130
In short, the Sydney region
has everything that you need

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.230
to build and scale what's next.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.510
And now, let's hear from
our local team in Australia

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.135
to learn what this
new region in Sydney

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.940
means for local customers.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.420
ANGELO JOSEPH: Hi,
I'm Angelo Joseph.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.970
I'm the head of
customer engineering

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.840
in Australia and New Zealand.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.200
My team and I help customers
in the adoption of Google Cloud

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.080
Platform solutions to
meet their business needs

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.290
and helping them
innovate into the future.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.670
We have thousands of customers
on our cloud platform.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.170
The likes of Woolworths,
Halfbrick, ingogo, News Corp,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:39.120
Fairfax, Service New South
Wales, and PwC to name a few.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.340
Customers such as
Rentokil Initial

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.970
are using our data flow and
publish and subscribe services

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.970
for IoT solutions for
facilities monitoring

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.640
for up to 10,000 customers.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.830
Others, such as
Monash University,

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.830
are using our Google App Engine
as an application service

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.180
platform.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.590
And digital natives,
like PaperCut,

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.570
are using big query for
analytics and reporting.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.570
What really excites me
about the Sydney region

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.750
is that it will allow
customers to store and process

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.410
data in Australia.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.520
Our performance testing
of the Sydney region

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.050
shows 40% to 90% reductions
in the round trip time latency

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.270
when serving
customers in Sydney as

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:25.180
compared to other regional
options in Taiwan, Japan,

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.750
Singapore, and India.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.790
I think customers
are going to love

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.260
having an even faster and
more local Google Cloud.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.995
GCP has been helping
customers in Australia

00:02:36.995 --> 00:02:40.060
and New Zealand for
more than five years,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.490
and with our sales teams based
in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane,

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.300
Auckland, we have always had
a local point of presence

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.490
to connect our local customers
to Google Cloud solutions.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:56.620
And now even more so that
we have a local GCP region.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.710
So we're really excited
to see what customers

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.470
will be building there.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.350
And finally, the
Google Cloud Summit

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.540
is coming to Australia
in September,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.135
so I look forward to
seeing you all there.

00:03:09.135 --> 00:03:10.260
NEAL MUELLER: That's right.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:10.821
Thanks.

00:03:10.821 --> 00:03:12.570
There's never been a
better time to get up

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:15.030
and running with
Google Cloud Platform.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.610
We think GCP is the
smart, secure cloud

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.380
to help move your
business forward.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.117
And with our new region in
Sydney, we're right next door.

00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:23.700
We're excited to see
what you're going

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.560
to build in the Sydney region.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.750
And remember to check out
the Google Cloud homepage

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.830
for upcoming summits near you.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.380
Thanks.

